{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792406937,"nonce":"8KlDk9ZOFt67vmRzu7b1iwqAjdA=","title":"GC trigger stays at 4x live up to 512 MB for a mid-size live set, and idle collection needs a quiet loop","message":"From a native ashui app (ashui git-bug ee667ca). With about 140 MB live the next trigger sat at 512 MB (x4.0), garbage floated up to it before a collection, and the macOS footprint reached 850 to 1300 MB; hl.Gc.major() after a page change took 4 to 25 ms and brought it to about 500 MB. A lower cap, or a smaller multiplier above some live size, would suit such apps. Separately, origin=idle collection never ran while the UI loop woke every 50 ms ([gc-idle]: idle 5 to 28 ms, busy 96 to 99 percent); it ran once the loop slept longer. The loop that never slept was ashui's and is fixed; no reproducer without ashui yet.","files":null}]}